{"type":"message","id":"738d70cc","parentId":"4749f0fe","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:10.485Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:22","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Analysis\n\nThis is **not a site plan or drawing** — it's a **Fire Sprinkler Hydraulics Calculation Report** (Page 12) for the **H+H Bellevue ED Ambulance Bay Addition**, generated by Elite Software on August 12, 2025.\n\n**There are no site dimensions, paving areas, utility locations, excavation areas, demo boundaries, or dimension callouts** in this document.\n\n### What This Document Contains:\n\n**Key Numeric Data Extracted:**\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| HMD Sprinkler Node | 101 |\n| Residual Pressure | 8.16 psi |\n| HMD Flow | 16.00 gpm |\n| System Type | Wet |\n| Coverage Area | 964.00 ft² |\n| Min Desired Density | 0.100 gpm/ft² |\n| Application Density | 0.320 gpm/ft² |\n| Area Per Sprinkler | 80.33 ft² |\n| Sprinkler Flow | 308.07 gpm |\n| Max Flow Velocity (Pipe 7-8) | 19.62 ft/sec |\n| Max Velocity Pressure (Pipe 7-8) | 2.59 psi |\n| Unique Pipe Sections | 25 |\n| Flowing Sprinklers | 12 |\n| Pipe System Water Volume | 42.11 gal |\n| Min Required Residual Pressure | 57.71 psi |\n| Demand Flow at Inflow Node | 308.07 gpm |\n\nThis would typically accompany MEP/fire protection drawings for the ambulance bay addition project."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_092.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052630479}}
