{"type":"message","id":"91505a35","parentId":"7c6ac313","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:54.777Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:27","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Flood Map Data Sheet\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Title:** FLOOD MAP DATA\n- **Sheet Number:** G-004.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue – ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION\n- **Location:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n\n## 2. Plan Type\nThis is a **FEMA Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) reference sheet**, not a traditional site/grading plan. It contains two FIRM panels showing the project location relative to flood zones.\n\n## 3. FIRM Panel Information\n- **Left panel:** Panel 0201F, Panel 20 of 47 — Map Number 36047C0201, revised **September 5, 2007**\n- **Right panel:** Panel 0201G, Panel 21 of 47 — Map Number 3604702010\n- **City/County:** New York, New York (New York, Bronx, Queens, and Kings Counties)\n\n## 4. Flood Zone Information\nThe legend identifies multiple flood zones including:\n- **Zone AE** — Special flood hazard area with base flood elevations\n- **Zone VE** — Coastal high hazard area\n- **Zone X** (shaded/unshaded) — Moderate/minimal flood hazard\n- **Coastal Barrier Resources System (CBRS) areas**\n\n**Project location** is noted as \"PARTIALLY LOCATED WITHIN ZONE AE\" and \"LOCATED WITHIN ZONE X\"\n\n## 5. Damage/Improvement Cost Valuation\n- **Estimated Market Value:** $593,243,000\n- **Actual Value Total:** $266,959,350\n- **Actual Value Land:** $140,865,750\n- **Calculated Market Value:** ~$280,208,000\n- **50% of Market Value:** $140,104,000\n- **Estimated Construction Cost** (per Accucost, 8/17/2021): **$75,639,899**\n\n**Conclusion:** $75,639,899 < $140,104,000 → **Property is NOT substantially improved"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_005.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052674772}}
{"type":"message","id":"4bbc6696","parentId":"91505a35","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:09.891Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:28","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan Analysis\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** LIFE SAFETY PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** G0.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n\n## 2. Scale and Dimensions\n- **Scale:** 1/8\" = 1'-0\" (both A8 Life Safety Plan and A6 Occupancy Load Plan)\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n\n## 3. Demo Boundaries\n- Note at lower left: **\"CONTINUATION OF EXISTING LINTEL AS SHOWN IN BOLD LINE FROM EXISTING CONDITION\"**\n- Dimension callout: **3'-5(±0) / 36'-11\"**\n- References to demolition/construction barriers and temporary partitions in the general notes\n\n## 4. Excavation Areas\n- No specific excavation areas identified on this sheet (this is a Life Safety Plan, not a site/demo plan)\n\n## 5. Dimension Callouts\n- **3'-5(±0) / 36'-11\"** (at grid area B)\n- Door schedules with dimensions:\n  - **Door ED-1-01:** Clear Width 4'-8\", Capacity 75\n  - **Door ED-1-02:** Clear Width 3'-3\", Capacity 45\n  - **Door ED-1-03:** Clear Width 2'-11\", Capacity 45\n- Room dimensions noted: **10'-0\" H.I.**, **7'-0\" H.I.**, **106'-8\" H.I.**\n\n## 6. Utility/Demo Information\n- Notes reference contractor providing **exhaust fans with HEPA filters** during demolition\n- **Temporary partitions** required during demolition/construction\n- **Construction barriers** with gasket hollow metal doors\n- Smoke compartment designations: **2.1**\n- Fire division designations shown: **1.1**\n\n## Summary\nThis is a **Life Safety Plan** (not a demolition or site plan), focused on egress, fire ratings, occupant loads, and smoke compartments"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_006.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052689886}}
{"type":"message","id":"7b897a58","parentId":"4bbc6696","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:22.589Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:29","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan Analysis: **1st Floor - Exit Discharge Plan**\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Title:** 1ST FLOOR - EXIT DISCHARGE PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** G-007.00\n- **Project:** ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION (H+H Bellevue)\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Demo Application Number:** MS-M00610279-I1\n\n## 2. Scale and Dimensions\n- **Scale:** 1/64\" = 1'-0\" (noted at viewport A1)\n- **Architect:** Array Architects, 200 Madison Avenue, 14th Floor, New York, NY 10016\n\n## 3. Compartment Dimensions (Existing Healthcare Occupancy)\n\n| Compartment | Square Footage | Occupancy Load | Distance to Smoke | Distance to Exit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G.1A/G.1B | 5,142 | 26 | 60' | 120' |\n| G.2 | 5,442 | 23 | 77' | 126' |\n| G.3 | 21,097 | 88 | 122' | 148' |\n| G.4 | 9,603 | 40 | ≤30 PAT. SL. | 140' |\n| G.5 | 11,309 | 48 | ≤30 PAT. SL. | 60' |\n| G.6 | 10,023 | 84 | ≤30 PAT. SL. | 139' |\n| G.7 | 3,431 | 29 | ≤30 PAT. SL. | 110' |\n| **TOTAL** | **66,047** | **338** | | |\n\n## 4. Existing Business Occupancy\n\n| Compartment | Sq. Ft. | Distance to Exit |\n|---|---|---|\n| GB.1A/GB.1B | 33,805 | 120' |\n| GB.2 |"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_007.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052702560}}
{"type":"message","id":"a5761559","parentId":"7b897a58","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:28.975Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me look at more pages to find the actual civil/site plans. Let me check pages that may have the C- series drawings.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:30","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_001.png","prompt":"Analyze this drawing. Identify the sheet title, drawing index, and list all the drawing sheets included in this project set. Look for civil/site drawings specifically."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:31","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_002.png","prompt":"Analyze this drawing and identify:\n1. Sheet title and number\n2. Site plan with dimensions\n3. Overall site boundaries\n4. Building location on site\n5. Paving and utility areas\n6. Any dimension callouts\nFocus on extracting specific numeric dimensions."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"image:32","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_003.png","prompt":"Analyze this drawing and identify:\n1. Sheet title and number\n2. Site demolition plan details\n3. Dimensions of demo areas\n4. Paving removal areas\n5. Any utility or storm drainage info\nFocus on extracting specific numeric dimensions for site demolition work."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"moonshot","model":"kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":40637,"output":290,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40927,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770052702589}}
{"type":"message","id":"901c90f0","parentId":"a5761559","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:41.681Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:30","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Drawing Analysis\n\n**Sheet Title:** COVER SHEET\n\n**Drawing Number:** T-001.00\n\n**Project:** H+H Bellevue — ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n**Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n\n**Issue:** Issued Solution for Bid | 09/25/25\n\n**Project No.:** 6629\n\n---\n\nUnfortunately, this image only shows the **cover sheet** (T-001.00) and does not include a visible drawing index/sheet list. The drawing index that would typically list all sheets in the set is either on a separate sheet or too small to read in this image.\n\n**Consultants identified** (which hint at discipline sets included):\n\n- **ARRAY Architects** – Architecture\n- **DVORI Engineering PLLC** – MEP Engineer\n- **Yisrael A. Seinuk, P.C.** – Structural Engineer\n- **FK & Associates** – Geotechnical & Civil Engineer (Elmwood Park, NJ)\n- **MG Engineering D.P.C.** – Medical Gas/Anti-Seismic/Utility Engineer\n- **Environmental Planning Management** – Environmental Engineer\n\n**Civil/Site Drawings:** Based on the involvement of **FK & Associates** (Geotechnical & Civil Engineer), civil/site drawings (likely prefixed **C-**) would be expected in this set, but the specific sheet list is not legible from this cover sheet image.\n\nTo identify the complete drawing index and specific civil/site sheets, I would need the **drawing index sheet** (likely T-001.01 or similar) or a higher-resolution image."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_001.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052721675}}
{"type":"message","id":"005ac48c","parentId":"901c90f0","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:18:58.140Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:31","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** \"SYMBOLS LEGEND, AND GENERAL NOTES\"\n- **Sheet Number:** G-001\n- **Project:** **ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION** at **H+H Bellevue** (462 First Avenue, New York, NY 10016)\n\n## 2. Site Plan with Dimensions\nThe sheet contains a **Project Location Map** showing the site in **Manhattan** near the East River, around the Bellevue Hospital area (E 34th Street / E 28th Street corridor). There is also an **Area Map** showing buildings labeled **BUILDING E, F, G, H** with the project location marked.\n\nNo detailed site plan with specific dimensions is provided on this sheet — this is a general notes/legend sheet.\n\n## 3. Overall Site Boundaries\nThe area map shows the hospital campus bounded approximately by:\n- **E 34th Street** (north)\n- **East River / FDR Drive** (east)\n- **E 28th Street** (south)\n- **First Avenue** (west)\n\n## 4. Building Location on Site\nThe project is located adjacent to **BUILDING H** (H+H Bellevue), with the ambulance bay addition situated between existing buildings on the campus.\n\n## 5. Paving and Utility Areas\nNot detailed on this sheet. Per the drawing list, relevant sheets include:\n- **C-100:** Site/Civil Plan\n- **C-101:** Grading and Drainage Plan\n\n## 6. Dimension Callouts\nThe **General Dimensioning** section defines conventions:\n- Center-to-center indicator: **symbol shown**\n- Face of surface indicator: **symbol shown**\n- Dimensions taken from **finish surface unless otherwise noted**\n- **\"±\"** indicates possible field variation\n- **\"CLEAR\"** = actual field dimension may be less than code minimum but not more than 1\" less\n- **\"HOLD\"** = dimension must be equal to indicated and maintained\n\n**No specific numeric site dimensions appear on this sheet.** Numeric dimensions would be found on sheets C-100, A-100, and A-200 series per the drawing list.\n\n---\n\n**Issued:** 09/25"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_002.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052738134}}
{"type":"message","id":"63faaea7","parentId":"005ac48c","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:19:11.119Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:32","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** BUILDING CODE SUMMARY\n- **Sheet Number:** G.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n## 2. Key Details\n\nThis is **not a site demolition plan** — it's a **Building Code Summary** sheet containing code requirements for renovations, building department notes, zoning analysis, fire ratings, and special inspections.\n\n## 3. What's Present\n\n- **Occupancy Classification:** H-2, I-2 (New Healthcare)\n- **Construction Classification:** Non-combustible, Type I-A / I-C\n- **Building Height:** Existing 20 stories / 210 ft\n- **Project Area:** Approx. 1,636 SF\n- **Zoning Analysis** with floor areas:\n  - Ground FL: 494 SF → 654 SF\n  - Residential (3rd floor): 394 SF → 396 SF\n  - Total: 948 SF → 947 SF\n  - Existing zoning gross floor area for Bellevue campus: **1,898,095 SF**\n- **Fire Ratings**, **Corridor/egress requirements**, **Code references** (1968 NYC Building Code)\n\n## 4. No Demolition/Paving/Utility Info\n\nThis sheet does **not contain**:\n- Site demolition plan details\n- Dimensions of demo areas\n- Paving removal areas\n- Utility or storm drainage information\n\nThese would typically be found on **C-series (Civil) or L-series (Landscape)** sheets such as C-100 or C-101 (Site Demolition Plan)."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_003.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052751092}}
