{"type":"message","id":"95c8e4a0","parentId":"6850551b","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:19:34.871Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:35","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: FA-101.00\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** FIRE ALARM FLOOR PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** FA-101.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue — **ED Ambulance Bay Addition**\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n- **Project No:** 6629\n- **Contract No:** 09/25/25\n\n## 2. Drawing Contents\nTwo views are shown:\n1. **Fire Alarm Plan** (Scale: 1/8\" = 1'-0\")\n2. **Fire Alarm Plan – FACP Location** (Scale: 1/8\" = 1'-0\")\n\n## 3. Floor Plan Layout\n- **Grid lines:** Numbered 1–8 (horizontal) and lettered A–F (vertical)\n- Key areas identified:\n  - **Ambulance Court** (grid E, between 6-7)\n  - **Existing Recreation Deck Above** (grid F, around 6)\n  - **Existing Emergency Canopy Above** (grid D-E, around 6)\n  - **New Ramp with Asphalt** (grid D-E area)\n  - **Replaced Wall** (grid E area)\n  - **Entrance Vestibule** (grid B, around 6)\n  - **Security Station** (grid B)\n  - **Cart Wash** (grid C)\n  - **Area of Work** (labeled near grid B-C, columns 2-3)\n  - **Existing Fire Alarm Panel (FACP)** location shown in Detail 2\n\n## 4. Fire Alarm Devices Noted\n- **Fire Detectors** (multiple locations marked)\n- **Staff Paging/Speakers**\n- **Hand/Wave Plate**\n- **Horn/Strobe** devices\n- **Audible/Visual appliances**\n- **A/C Plug on Pedestal**\n- **Autoexpressor (approx 12 SF)**\n- **Hose Bibb**\n- **Bike Rack**\n- **"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_044.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052774838}}
{"type":"message","id":"53557d32","parentId":"95c8e4a0","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:19:50.188Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:36","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: SP-102.00\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Title:** EXISTING GROUND FLOOR SPRINKLER PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** SP-102.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue — **ED Ambulance Bay Addition**\n- **Location:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No:** 6829\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n- **Scale:** NTS (Not to Scale)\n\n## 2. Foundation/Structural Details\nThis is a **fire protection/sprinkler plan**, not a structural drawing. No foundation or structural details are shown.\n\n## 3. Canopy Structure Dimensions\nNo canopy dimensions are visible on this sheet.\n\n## 4. Steel Framing Sizes\nNot applicable — this is a sprinkler plan. No steel framing sizes shown.\n\n## 5. Concrete Dimensions\nNot shown on this sheet.\n\n## What IS Shown\n- **Sprinkler branch line sizing schedule** (with pipe sizes ranging from 1\" to potentially 2\"+)\n- Sprinkler head locations throughout the existing ground floor\n- Labels: **\"PEDIATRICS WALK-IN\"**, **\"ADULT EMERGENCY WALK-IN ENTRANCE\"**, **\"To DRY ROOM\"**\n- **Yellow highlighted area** appears to indicate the new work/renovation zone for the ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- Sprinkler branch pipe sizing schedule with number of sprinklers per line size\n- Reference to pipe sizes including **1\", 1¼\", 1½\", 2\"**\n- Note referencing **\"NEW SPACE\"**\n\n## Consultants Listed\n- **Severud Associates** — Structural Engineer\n- **Ysrael A. Seinuk, P.C.** — Civil Engineer\n- **MG Engineering** — MEP/FP Engineer\n- **Albert Schwimowitz & Partners** — additional consultant\n\n**Note:** For structural dimensions, steel framing, concrete, and canopy details, refer to the **S-series (structural)** and **A-series (architectural)** sheets in this drawing set."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_078.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052790182}}
{"type":"message","id":"ba552772","parentId":"53557d32","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:20:04.203Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:37","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Name:** ASBESTOS ABATEMENT PARTIAL GROUND FLOOR PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** H-101.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue — **ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION**\n- **Full Project Title:** BELLEVUE HOSPITAL ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION\n- **Project No.:** 68/25/25328\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Issue:** ISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID 09/25/2025\n- **Architect:** ARRAY ARCHITECTS, 200 Madison Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n\n## 2. Asbestos Abatement Table (Key Numeric Data)\n\n| Room | Asbestos Material | Removal Method | Linear Ft | Sq. Ft. |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Emergency Dept. Triage Area | Presumed asbestos containing spray-on fireproofing (allowance) | Full containment procedure or ACP-9 variance | — | 50 |\n| Ambulance Bay Vestibule | Presumed asbestos containing spray-on fireproofing (allowance) | Full containment procedure or ACP-9 variance | — | 100 |\n| Emergency Dept. Critical Care Area | Presumed asbestos containing spray-on fireproofing (allowance) | Full containment procedure or ACP-9 variance | — | 130 |\n| **TOTAL** | | | | **280** |\n\n## 3. Building Layout and Major Areas\n\nThe plan shows a **Partial Ground Floor** with these major zones:\n- **PEDIATRIC EMERGENCY SERVICE** (upper/north portion)\n- **EMERGENT CARE** (left/west, grid lines 1-4, rows 12-13)\n- **IMMEDIATE CARE** (center, areas 5-6)\n- **URGENT CARE** (right/east center)\n- **CRITICAL CARE** (lower left, rows 1-5)\n- **AMBULANCE ENTRANCE** (lower center)\n- **UNASSIGNED** area (right side)\n-"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_126.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052804197}}
