{"type":"message","id":"549154ab","parentId":"9e20477d","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:21:42.942Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:48","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Sheet Analysis: FO-001\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-001\n- **Sheet Title:** FOUNDATION - COVER SHEET AND DRAWING LIST\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition, 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No:** 6629\n- **Date:** 06/06/2022\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n\n## 2. Drawing List\n| Sheet | Description |\n|-------|------------|\n| FO-001 | Foundation - Cover Sheet and Drawing List |\n| FO-002 | Foundation General Notes |\n| FO-101 | Foundation Plan |\n| FO-200 | Typical Foundation Details |\n| FO-201 | Typical Foundation Details |\n| FO-300 | Foundation Sections |\n\n## 3. Loading Schedule\n| Floor | Slab | Finishes | Fill and Hangers | Ceiling and Partition | Dead | Live | Total |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|------|------|------|-------|\n| High Density Storage | 150 psf | 10 psf | 0 psf | 15 psf | 175 psf | 100 psf | — |\n\n## 4. Earthquake Design Criteria\n- **Seismic Importance Factor:** 1.25\n- **Seismic Occupancy:** D\n- **Short Period SS:** 0.389g\n- **1 Second Period:** 0.73%g\n- **Site Class:** D\n- **Design Short Period SDS:** 1.0075g\n- **Base Shear:** V=20 KIP\n\n## 5. Wind Design Data\n- **Basic Wind Speed:** 98 MPH\n- **Wind Importance Factor:** 1.15\n- **Wind Exposure:** Category C\n- **Components and Cladding:** 30 PSF\n\n## 6. Special Inspections (Structural References)\n- Structural Steel - Welding: BC 1705.2.1\n- Structural Steel - Bolting: BC 1705.2.2\n-"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_112.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052902936}}
{"type":"message","id":"96722ee1","parentId":"549154ab","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:21:57.554Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:49","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: FO-002\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-002\n- **Sheet Title:** FOUNDATION GENERAL NOTES\n- **Project:** ED Ambulance Bay Addition (H+H Bellevue)\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n\n## 2. Structural Plan or Details\nThis is a **general notes sheet**, not a structural plan. It contains:\n- Earthwork Notes\n- Foundation Notes\n- Excavation notes\n- Concrete and Steel Reinforcement Notes\n- Codes and Tests\n- Anchor Bolts Specification\n- Miscellaneous Notes\n\n## 3. Steel Member Sizes\nNo specific steel member sizes are shown on this notes sheet.\n\n## 4. Canopy Framing Dimensions\nNo canopy framing dimensions on this sheet.\n\n## 5. Dimension Callouts (from notes)\n\n**Concrete Strength:**\n- Pile caps/grade beams: **4000 PSI at 28 days**, stone concrete\n- Plinth/walls: **4000 PSI at 28 days**, stone concrete\n- Slab on grade: **4000 PSI at 28 days**, stone concrete\n\n**Reinforcement:**\n- Steel reinforcement: **60,000 PSI** (Grade 60, ASTM A615)\n- Welded wire fabric: minimum yield strength **60,000 PSI**\n\n**Key Dimensions from Notes:**\n- Maintain ground water level minimum **2 feet** below excavation during construction\n- Ground water levels maintained at least **2 ft** below proposed foundations\n- Piles supported on **#4W KIP** capacity piles with **14 in** diameter x **1/4W\"** thick\n- Vertical construction joints at least **4'-0\"** from any supporting column\n- Slab on grade: **FF 25 / FL 25**\n- Void formers: rigid **25.0 PSI**; compressible **12.0 PSI**\n- Excavation backfill compacted to **95%** levels\n\n**Project Info:**\n- **Project No:** 6629\n- **Date:**"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_113.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052917548}}
{"type":"message","id":"dd61528b","parentId":"96722ee1","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:22:12.527Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:50","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: FO-101\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** FOUNDATION PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-101\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No:** 6629\n- **Date:** 06/06/25\n- **Scale:** 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n\n## 2. Structural Details with Dimensions\n- **Plan Title:** GROUND FLOOR (ACTUAL 1ST FLOOR)\n- Key spans: **13524** (repeated multiple times between grid lines)\n- Dimensions: **9'-10 1/4\"**, **9'-10 1/4\"**, **9'-10 1/4\"** (repeated bay spacing)\n- **49'-0 1/2\"** overall dimension\n- **18'-6 1/4\"** and **37'-0 3/4\"** dimensions noted\n- **25'-10 3/4\"** dimension at grid D\n- Member designations: **PC-1**, **GB-1**, **GB-2**, **DB-1**, **S-12**\n- **FD-300** and **FD-300** footing designations\n- **(TF) - T1** notation\n\n## 3. Foundation Details\n\n**Foundation Notes:**\n1. Concrete foundation slab shall be 12\" thick, c/o 6 x 6, on plus fc = 4000 PSI, top and bottom reinforcing mat shall be #6@12\" OC continuous U.O.N.\n2. For general notes, see FG-001\n3. For foundation typical details, see FG-000 drawings\n4. Top of pile caps are -1'-0\" below top of slab U.O.N.\n5. All grade beams are -1'-0\" below top of slab U.O.N.\n\n## 4. Grade Beam Schedule\n\n| Mark | Size (B x H) | Bottom Bars | Top L. Bars | Top F.L. Bars | Top R.E. Bars | Stirrups Size |"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_114.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052932487}}
