{"type":"message","id":"44bf446d","parentId":"511b0659","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:22:34.676Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:51","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: FO-200\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-200\n- **Sheet Title:** TYPICAL FOUNDATION DETAILS\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n- **Project No:** 6629\n- **Date:** 06/06/25\n\n## 2. Structural Details Identified\n\nThe sheet contains **13 details (A through M):**\n\n| Detail | Title |\n|--------|-------|\n| A | Typical Grade Beam Reinforcing Detail |\n| B | Typical Sleeve Penetrations Through Concrete Beams |\n| C | Typical Detail of Reinforcement at Change in Beam Elevations |\n| D | Typical Sleeve Penetrations Through Grade Beams |\n| E | Typical Conduit Concrete Encasement Detail |\n| F | Typical Wall Detail Supported by Slab on Grade |\n| G | Typical Wall Intersection Details |\n| H | Typical Curb Detail |\n| I | Typical Concrete Slab Joints (Isolation Joint, Saw-Cut Control Joint) |\n| J | Column Joint Detail |\n| K | Typical Detail of Adjacent Footing on Soils |\n| L | Typical Vertical Construction Joint in Wall |\n| M | Typical Slab on Ground Construction Joint |\n\n## 3. Key Dimensions and Callouts\n\n**Grade Beam (Detail A):**\n- #6 @ 2'-0\" stirrups (typical)\n- Bars not to extend 60x bar diameter beyond end of beam\n- 2#11 bars, #5 stirrups noted\n- Clear span of beam marked at PER (per structural)\n- 1'-0\" minimum dimensions noted\n- 10 equal spaces noted for stirrup layout\n\n**Sleeve Penetrations (Detail B):**\n- Sleeve height ≤ 1/3 diameter\n- 2\"-3\" clearances noted (2½\", 3\")\n- Add 3 sets of stirrups, 2"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_115.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052954669}}
{"type":"message","id":"05d58998","parentId":"44bf446d","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:22:49.420Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:52","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Sheet Analysis: FO-201\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Title:** TYPICAL FOUNDATION DETAILS\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-201\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 06/06/25\n\n## 2. Structural Sections/Details\n\n| Detail | Title | Scale |\n|--------|-------|-------|\n| **N/FO-201** | Typical Reinforcing at Opening and Misc Details | N.T.S |\n| **O/FO-201** | Horizontal Section Showing Placement of Wall Reinforcement | N.T.S |\n| **P/FO-201** | Typical One-Way Slab | N.T.S |\n| **Q/FO-201** | Typical Slab Penetration with Sleeve Diameter Less Than 6\" | N.T.S |\n| **R/FO-201** | Typical Concrete Pad Detail | N.T.S |\n\n## 3. Foundation Sections with Dimensions\n- **Wall reinforcement:** #4/#5 bars at various spacings\n- **Buttress sections** shown with outline of buttress where required\n- **Foundation footing** dimensions: 3'-0\", 2'-0\" referenced\n- **Bottom of footing** elevation callouts\n- **Lap splices:** @ mid span - see notes (typ.)\n- **Cover requirements referenced** via notes\n\n## 4. Concrete and Steel Details\n- **Lap splice:** See notes for horizontal and vertical bars\n- **#4DL bars** - see sections\n- **#4DL 1-#4 bar around each opening** (typ.)\n- **Rebar at slab:** For slab & reinf see plan\n- **Concrete pad:** #4@12 (typ.) all around\n- **One-way slab temp. reinf table:**\n  - 4\" slab: #4 @ 12\"\n  - 5\" slab: #4 @ 12\"\n  - 6\" slab: #4 @ 12\"\n  - 7\""}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_116.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052969413}}
{"type":"message","id":"69305250","parentId":"05d58998","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:23:03.089Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:53","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: FO-300\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Sheet Title:** FOUNDATION SECTIONS\n- **Sheet Number:** FO-300\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 06/06/25\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n\n## 2. Structural Details\n\n### Section 1 (FO-300, Scale: 3/4\" = 1'-0\")\n- Ground Floor (Actual 1st Floor) elevation: 13'-1 1/2\"\n- Top of pile cap elevation: 1'-6\" below top of slab\n- Grade beam (GB-1) with top and bottom bars continuous through pile cap\n- (4) #8 TYP edge of slab\n- Slab depth approximately 24\"\n\n### Section 2 (FO-300, Scale: 3/4\" = 1'-0\")\n- Ground Floor (Actual 1st Floor): 13'-1 1/2\"\n- (4) #8 TYP edge of slab\n- Grade beam top and bottom bars continuous; see schedule for reinforcement requirements\n\n### Section 3 - Detail (FO-300, Scale: 3/4\" = 1'-0\")\n- Ground Floor (Actual 1st Floor): 13'-1 1/2\"\n- Grade beam continuous above slab for GB-2 locations\n- #6 @ 12\" OC dowels, TYP\n- See grade beam schedule for size, bar size, and spacing\n- GB-2 designation\n\n## 3. Steel Connection Details\n- (4) #8 rebar TYP at edge of slab (multiple sections)\n- #6 @ 12\" OC dowels typical\n\n## 4. Foundation Details\n\n### Pile Cap PC-1 (Detail 4, Scale: 3/4\" = 1'-0\")\n- **Notes:**\n  1. Depth = 2'-0\"\n  2. Reinf: 4 #8 each way"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_117.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052983083}}
