{"type":"message","id":"a382413f","parentId":"302c6021","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:24:06.153Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:56","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Drawing Analysis: A-501.00\n\n## 1. Sheet Title and Number\n- **Title:** REFLECTED CEILING PLAN AND ROOF PLAN\n- **Sheet Number:** A-501.00\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Issue:** ISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n\n## 2. Roof Plan Dimensions and Area\n- From Architectural Keynotes: **A6** references \"AREA OF NEW ROOFING (ROOFING TYPE 1, SEE DETAIL 5/A-503). CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE NEW R-31 (5.5\" MIN THICKNESS) & NEW ROOF MEMBRANE SLOPED TO ROOF DRAIN\"\n- The canopy roof plan (bottom left, detail **A8**) is at **1/4\" = 1'-0\"** scale\n- Grid spacing dimensions visible along grid lines but specific numeric roof dimensions are difficult to read at this resolution\n\n## 3. Canopy Dimensions\n- **A8: EMERGENCY ENTRANCE CANOPY ROOF PLAN** at 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n- The canopy spans between gridlines **A** through approximately **D.B** (north-south) and gridlines **5** through **8** (east-west)\n- Dimension string shows approximately **36'-0\"** span visible near grid line A\n- Keynote references \"UNDERSIDE OF CANOPY ROOF EXISTING CEILING 4 CONTG TO REMAIN\" and \"RED CURTAIN\"\n- Canopy slope noted: **CRICKET 1/4\" PER FT. SLOPE (TYP.)**\n\n## 4. Structural Grid\nGrid lines identified:\n- **North-South (letters):** A, A.B, B.B, C, C.B, D, D.B, E, E.B, F, F.B, G.B, H.B, I.B\n- **East-West (numbers):** 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 5.B, 6, 6.B,"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_021.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770053046145}}
{"type":"message","id":"5318bb92","parentId":"a382413f","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:24:06.162Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"read:57","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"3.B\n4.B\n2.B\n5.B\n1.B\nA.B\nB.B\nC.B\nE.B\nG.B\n6.B\nD.B\nF.B\n2.B1\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W12X30\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X146\n(E)W14X22\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X146\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W16X31\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W12X30\n(E)W27X84\n(E)W14X30\n(E)W12X30\n(E)W27X84\nW8X35\n1\nS-300\nW8X24\nW8X24\nHSS6X6X5/8\nHSS6X6X5/8\nW8X24\nW8X24\nHSS6X6X5/8\nW8X35\nW8X35\nW8X35\nW8X35\n2L4X4X1/2X3/8\nBELOW\nBELOW\nBELOW\nT/STL EL 21' - 7\" TYP\nP1\nP1\nP1\nP1\nP1\nH1\nH1\nH1\nH1\nH1\n6\" MASONRY WALL \nREINFORCED WITH \n#4@32\" OC, TYP\n13'-9\"\n2'-7\"\n9'-4 1/4\"\n20'-6\"\nO\nS-201\nSim\nO\nS-201\nSim\nEXISTING EMERGENCY ROOM \nBUILDING ENTRYWAY\nTOW EL 27' - 2\" TYP\n(E)W16X31\n0\"\n4'-4 1/2\"\n6'-4\"\n4'-4 1/2\"\n4'-2\"\n9'-6 1/4\"\n7'-6\"\nLOCATION OF MECHANICAL \nEQUIPMENT SUPPORT TO \nBE VERIFIED WITH EXISTING \nFRAMING LAYOUT IN FIELD \nW8X24\nC8X13.75\nC8X13.75\n2'-3\"\n2L4X4X1/2X3/8\n2L4X4X1/2X3/8\n2L4X4X1/2X3/8\n2L4X4X1/2X3/8\nP2\n40'-11 1/4\"\nC8X13.75\n5\nS-300\n2'-8 1/4\"\n6\nS-300\nHSS6X4X3/8\nBELOW\nT/STL 20' - 2\"\nHSS4X4X3/8\nC8X13.75\nC6X13\nC6X13\nC6X13\n1'-11 1/4\"\n2'-8 1/2\"\n11 1/2\"\n3'-9 1/4\"\n3'-0 1/4\"\nS-101\n3\nS-101\n4\nG\nS-200\nSim\n4'-4 1/4\"\n7\nS-300\nW8X10\nPOST/HANGER ABOVE OR BELOW, SEE S400 SERIES FOR \nTYPICAL REQ.\n#\nSTEEL BEAM\nSHEAR CONNECTION\nMOMENT CONNECTION\nEXISTING COLUMN LINE\nEXISTING STEEL BEAM\n(E)W8X10\nTOP OF SLAB ELEVATION\n+0'-0\"\nINDICATES STEP DOWN\nINDICATES SLOPE DOWN OR UP\nLEGEND\na.\nb.\nc.\nd.\ne.\nf.\ng.\nh.\ni.\nNOTES:\n1. \nTOP OF CANOPY STEEL IS 27'-2\" U.O.N\n2. \nREFER TO S001 FOR GENERAL NOTES.\n3. \nFOR CONNECTION DESIGN USE V=15 KIPS FOR ALL SHEAR CONNECTIONS AND M=35 KIP-FT FOR ALL MOMENT CONNECTIONS SHOWN ON PLAN\n4. \nCOORDINATE ALL SLAB OPENINGS, SLOPES, SLEEVES, DEPRESSIONS, EDGE  DIMENSIONS AND\nCURBS WITH ARCHITECT, CIVIL, M.E.P. AND ALL OTHER PRIME CONTRACTORS.\n5. \nCOORDINATE ALL DIMENSIONS, LOCATIONS AND WALL OPENINGS WITH ARCHITECT, CIVIL, M.E.P. \nAND ALL OTHER PRIME CONTRACTORS.\n6. \nREFER TO ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS FOR MASONRY WALL AND MASONRY WALL SHELF ELEVATIONS AND CONFIGURATION.\n7. \nINDICATES HSS 6X6X5/8\" POST \n8. \nINDICATES HSS 4X4X3/8\" POST \n9. \nINDICATES L2X2X3/8\" POST\n10. \nINDICATES WT4X24 HANGER \n11. \nFOR MASONRY TYPICAL DETAILS SEE S201\n12. \nLOCATION OF FRAMING AROUND BALLISTIC DOOR ENTRYWAYS TO BE COORDINATE/CONFIRMED WITH MANUFACTURER. \nP1\nH1\nP2\nP3\nW8X24\nC8X13.75\nC8X13.75\nL3X3X1/2\nL3X3X1/2\nL3X3X1/2\nBELOW\nBELOW\nBELOW\nT/STL 28' - 3\"\nT/STL 27' - 11\"\nT/STL 28' - 3\"\nL3X3X1/2 T/STL 28' - 1\"\nP3\nP3\nP3\nP3\n7\nS-300\n2'-1 3/4\"\n3'-10 1/4\"\n5\nS-300\nBELOW\nC8X13.75\nBELOW\nC8X13.75\nC6X13\nL2X2X3/16\nC6X13\nL2X2X3/16\nC6X13\nL2X2X3/16\nL2X2X3/16\nBELOW\nBELOW\nBELOW\nT/STL 30' - 10\"\nT/STL 33' - 9\"\nT/STL 30' - 11\"\nT/STL 30' - 11\"\nP3\nP3\nP3\nP3\n1'-0\"\n10\"\n200 MADISON AVENUE, 14TH FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY 10016\n212-689-3110\nARRAY-ARCHITECTS.COM\nPROJECT NO.\nDATE\nCONTRACT NO.\nCON/REF NO.\nF\nE\nD\nC\nB\nA\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n1\nC  COPYRIGHT - 2021 ARRAY ARCHITECTS\nIN COLLABORATION WITH:\nDOSHI ENGINEERING PLLC\nMEP ENGINEER\n350 SEVENTH AVENUE, 15th FLOOR,\nNEW YORK, NY 10001\nPHONE: 718 896 9324\nPROJECT:\nISSUES:\nSEAL:\nKEYPLAN:\nYSRAEL A. SEINUK, P.C.\nSTRUCTURAL ENGINEER\n228 EAST 45TH STREET, 2ND FLOOR\nNEW YORK, NY  10017\nPHONE: 212 687 2233\nYU & ASSOCIATES\nGEOTECHNICAL & CIVIL ENGINEER\n611 RIVER DRIVE\nELMWOOD PARK, NY  07407\nPHONE: 201 791 0057\nMG ENGINEERING D.P.C.\nMEDICAL EQ, AV/IT, SECURITY ENGINEER\n116 WEST 32ND STREET\nNEW YORK, NY  10001\nPHONE: 212 643 9055  \nENVIRONMENTAL PLANNING \nMANAGEMENT\nENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER\n1983 MARCUS AVENUE, SUITE 109\nLAKE SUCCESS, NY  11042\nPHONE: 516 328 1194 \n9/24/2