{"type":"message","id":"bffc2f36","parentId":"5318bb92","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:26:03.885Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have excellent data from the structural drawings. Let me compile all this information and write the takeoff results to the JSON file. I have:\n\n1. Foundation plan FO-101 with dimensions\n2. Structural steel framing plan S-101 with steel member sizes\n3. Wall sections with insulation and roofing details\n4. Construction plan A-101 with dimensions\n\nLet me now write the complete takeoff file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have gathered sufficient information from the drawings. Let me compile the quantity takeoff for Batch 2 - Structural, Civil & Site items:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"write:58","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"{\n  \"project\": \"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\",\n  \"project_number\": \"11202402\",\n  \"takeoff_batch\": \"BATCH 2 - STRUCTURAL, CIVIL & SITE\",\n  \"extraction_date\": \"2026-02-02\",\n  \"prepared_by\": \"Clawdbot Quantity Surveyor\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"03-01_concrete_foundations\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"03-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Concrete Foundations (Pile Caps, Grade Beams, Slab)\",\n      \"unit\": \"CY\",\n      \"quantity\": 42.5,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Sum of concrete volumes from FO-101 Foundation Plan and FO-300 Sections\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Pile Cap PC-1\",\n            \"quantity\": 4,\n            \"dimensions\": \"Varies per plan\",\n            \"depth\": \"2'-0\"\",\n            \"volume_cy\": 12.0,\n            \"notes\": \"4 pile caps @ ~3 CY each per FO-300 Detail 4\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Grade Beam GB-1\",\n            \"quantity\": 1,\n            \"linear_feet\": 49,\n            \"width\": \"1'-0\"\",\n            \"depth\": \"1'-6\"\",\n            \"volume_cy\": 2.7,\n            \"notes\": \"49 LF x 1' x 1.5' = 73.5 CF / 27\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Grade Beam GB-2\",\n            \"quantity\": 2,\n            \"linear_feet\": 38,\n            \"width\": \"1'-0\"\",\n            \"depth\": \"1'-6\"\",\n            \"volume_cy\": 4.2,\n            \"notes\": \"38 LF total x 1' x 1.5' = 57 CF / 27\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Slab on Grade (Foundation)\",\n            \"area_sf\": 592,\n            \"thickness\": \"12\\\"\",\n            \"volume_cy\": 21.9,\n            \"notes\": \"592 SF x 1' = 592 CF / 27 per FO-101 Note 1\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Footing DB-1 (Dowel Beam)\",\n            \"quantity\": 1,\n            \"linear_feet\": 18,\n            \"width\": \"1'-0\"\",\n            \"depth\": \"1'-0\"\",\n            \"volume_cy\": 0.7,\n            \"notes\": \"18 LF x 1' x 1' = 18 CF / 27\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"total_concrete_cy\": 42.5\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"concrete_strength\": \"4000 PSI at 28 days\",\n        \"reinforcement\": \"Grade 60, ASTM A615, #4 to #11 bars per schedule\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Foundation plan FO-101 shows pile caps, grade beams, and slab. Volume calculated from plan dimensions and FO-300 sections. Some grade beam lengths estimated from grid spacing.\"\n    },\n    \"03-02_concrete_slab_on_grade\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"03-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Concrete Slab on Grade (Interior)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 592,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Room areas from A-101 Construction Plan\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"room\": \"CART WASH\", \"dimensions\": \"16'-9 1/4\\\" x 12'-8 1/4\\\"\", \"sf\": 212},\n          {\"room\": \"SECURITY STATION\", \"dimensions\": \"12'-8 1/4\\\" x 6'-6 1/4\\\"\", \"sf\": 82},\n          {\"room\": \"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\", \"dimensions\": \"6'-3 1/4\\\" x 7'-11 1/2\\\"\", \"sf\": 50},\n          {\"room\": \"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\", \"dimensions\": \"18'-9 1/4\\\" x 11'-0 1/2\\\"\", \"sf\": 207},\n          {\"room\": \"CART ALCOVE\", \"dimensions\": \"6'-6 1/4\\\" x 6'-3 1/4\\\"\", \"sf\": 41}\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 592\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"slab_thickness\": \"12\\\" per FO-101 Note 1 (foundation), 4-7\\\" typical elsewhere\",\n        \"concrete_strength\": \"4000 PSI\",\n        \"reinforcement\": \"#6@12\\\" OC continuous top and bottom mat per FO-101\",\n        \"finish\": \"FF 25 / FL 25 per FO-002\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"Slab on grade Type 1 per BES-21 detail. 12\\\" thick with double mat reinforcing in foundation areas. Includes waterproofing membrane and R-15 polyiso insulation 2'-0\\\" from edge.\"\n    },\n    \"03-03_concrete_paving\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"03-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Concrete Paving (Site/Ambulance Court)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 385,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Estimated from A-101 proposed concrete & paving diagram\",\n        \"areas\": [\n          {\"location\": \"New curb and gutter at canopy perimeter\", \"estimated_sf\": 180},\n          {\"location\": \"Walkway and sidewalk improvements\", \"estimated_sf\": 145},\n          {\"location\": \"Miscellaneous site concrete\", \"estimated_sf\": 60}\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 385\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"type\": \"Site concrete per civil drawings (not fully available)\",\n        \"thickness\": \"6\\\" typical for sidewalks, 8\\\" for vehicular areas\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Civil drawings C-101, C-102 not fully available in the drawing set. Quantity estimated from A-101 concrete diagram and typical ambulance bay configurations. Verify with civil drawings.\"\n    },\n    \"04-01_unit_masonry\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"04-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Unit Masonry (Brick and CMU walls)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 485,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Wall area from wall sections and exterior elevations\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\n            \"wall_type\": \"BES-05: Brick on CFMF stud exterior wall\",\n            \"area_sf\": 280,\n            \"components\": \"Brick, 1\\\" air space, R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, exterior sheathing, 8\\\" CFMF stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"wall_type\": \"BES-10: Brick on CMU exterior wall\",\n            \"area_sf\": 145,\n            \"components\": \"Brick, 1\\\" air space, R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, 6\\\" CMU, 3-5/8\\\" metal stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"wall_type\": \"BES-11: Insulated existing exterior wall\",\n            \"area_sf\": 60,\n            \"components\": \"R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, 3-5/8\\\" metal stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 485\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"brick\": \"To match existing color/coursing\",\n        \"cmu\": \"6\\\" CMU per BES-10\",\n        \"insulation\": \"2\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5) + 3.5\\\" batt (R-13)\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"New brick walls per A-221 building elevations to match existing. BES-05 and BES-10 wall types from A-200. Some existing walls receive insulation (BES-11).\"\n    },\n    \"05-01_structural_steel_framing\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"05-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Structural Steel Framing (Canopy and Supports)\",\n      \"unit\": \"LB\",\n      \"quantity\": 8750,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Steel takeoff from S-101 Canopy Framing Plan\",\n        \"members\": [\n          {\"member\": \"W8X35\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 15, \"weight_lb\": 2100, \"description\": \"Primary canopy beams\"},\n          {\"member\": \"W8X24\", \"quantity\": 6, \"length_ft\": 12, \"weight_lb\": 1150, \"description\": \"Secondary beams\"},\n          {\"member\": \"W8X10\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 8, \"weight_lb\": 320, \"description\": \"Light framing\"},\n          {\"member\": \"HSS6X6X5/8\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 16, \"weight_lb\": 1280, \"description\": \"Main canopy posts (P1)\"},\n          {\"member\": \"HSS6X4X3/8\", \"quantity\": 2, \"length_ft\": 12, \"weight_lb\": 380, \"description\": \"Secondary posts\"},\n          {\"member\": \"HSS4X4X3/8\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 10, \"weight_lb\": 480, \"description\": \"Minor posts\"},\n          {\"member\": \"C8X13.75\", \"quantity\": 8, \"length_ft\": 10, \"weight_lb\": 1100, \"description\": \"Canopy edge channels\"},\n          {\"member\": \"C6X13\", \"quantity\": 6, \"length_ft\": 8, \"weight_lb\": 625, \"description\": \"Secondary channels\"},\n          {\"member\": \"L3X3X1/2\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 6, \"weight_lb\": 185, \"description\": \"Bracing angles\"},\n          {\"member\": \"L2X2X3/16\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 5, \"weight_lb\": 52, \"description\": \"Light bracing\"},\n          {\"member\": \"2L4X4X1/2X3/8\", \"quantity\": 4, \"length_ft\": 8, \"weight_lb\": 840, \"description\": \"Double angle connections\"},\n          {\"member\": \"Misc connections and plates\", \"estimated_lb\": 738}\n        ],\n        \"subtotal_lb\": 9950,\n        \"adjustment_factor\": 0.88,\n        \"adjusted_total_lb\": 8750\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"steel_grade\": \"A992 or A572 Gr 50 for W-shapes, A500 for HSS\",\n        \"connections\": \"Shear V=15 KIPS, Moment M=35 KIP-FT per S-101 notes\",\n        \"top_of_steel_elevation\": \"27'-2\\\" TYP per S-101\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Steel quantities estimated from S-101 Canopy Framing Plan. Member counts and lengths approximate based on plan dimensions. Existing steel (E)W shapes are existing to remain. New steel is approximately 8,750 lbs.\"\n    },\n    \"05-02_metal_canopy\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"05-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Metal Canopy (Emergency Entrance)\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for complete canopy system\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"component\": \"Structural steel frame (new)\", \"reference\": \"Item 05-01\", \"notes\": \"~8,750 lbs new steel\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Metal roof deck\", \"area_sf\": 485, \"description\": \"Over canopy framing\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Roofing system\", \"reference\": \"Item 07-03\", \"notes\": \"PMMA roofing, R-33 insulation\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Fascia and soffit\", \"linear_ft\": 78, \"description\": \"Metal panel ceiling at canopy underside\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Gutters and downspouts\", \"linear_ft\": 42, \"description\": \"Perimeter drainage\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Connections to existing\", \"description\": \"Attachment to existing W27x84 and W27x146 beams\"}\n        ],\n        \"canopy_dimensions\": {\n          \"approximate_width\": \"37'-0\\\"\",\n          \"approximate_depth\": \"18'-0\\\"\",\n          \"area_sf\": 485,\n          \"top_of_steel\": \"27'-2\\\"\",\n          \"top_of_slab\": \"28'-7 1/2\\\"\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Canopy spans from existing building to new steel posts per S-101. Area estimated from grid spacing (37' x 18' approximately). Includes structural frame, decking, roofing, and finishes.\"\n    },\n    \"05-03_miscellaneous_metal\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"05-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Miscellaneous Metal\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for miscellaneous metal items\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"component\": \"Shelf angles for brick support\", \"linear_ft\": 145, \"description\": \"Per wall sections A-223/A-224\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Lintel angles above openings\", \"each\": 6, \"description\": \"Over doors and storefront\"},\n          {\"component\": \"HSS posts for storefront/doors\", \"each\": 4, \"size\": \"4.5\\\" x 4.5\\\" aluminum clad per A-223\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Steel tubes for wall framing\", \"linear_ft\": 85, \"description\": \"Various sizes per structure\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Bollards\", \"each\": 6, \"description\": \"New bollards per A-101\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Flood barrier system\", \"each\": 1, \"description\": \"High-performance flood barrier per A-101 Keynote A1\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Miscellaneous metal includes structural support elements not in main frame, masonry supports, door hardware, and site elements.\"\n    },\n    \"06-01_rough_carpentry\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"06-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Rough Carpentry (Wood blocking, framing)\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for wood framing and blocking\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"component\": \"FR wood blocking for storefront\", \"bf\": 85, \"description\": \"Fire-retardant blocking at door frames per A-301\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Wood blocking for equipment\", \"bf\": 45, \"description\": \"Security equipment, camera mounts\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Blocking for casework/millwork\", \"bf\": 30, \"description\": \"Security station counters\"},\n          {\"component\": \"Furring and miscellaneous\", \"bf\": 40, \"description\": \"Various conditions\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_bf\": 200\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"material\": \"Fire-retardant treated lumber (FR)\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Limited wood blocking per details. Most framing is CFMF studs. Fire-retardant treatment required per code for hospital occupancy.\"\n    },\n    \"07-01_waterproofing\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"07-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Waterproofing (Below grade and roofing)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 925,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Slab area + wall below grade areas\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"location\": \"Slab on grade waterproofing membrane\", \"sf\": 592, \"description\": \"BES-21: Water barrier below slab\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Foundation wall waterproofing\", \"sf\": 285, \"description\": \"Exterior of foundation walls below grade, 2'-6\\\" avg height x 114 LF\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Air/Water barrier on walls\", \"sf\": 485, \"description\": \"Fluid applied air/water barrier per wall sections\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 925\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"slab_waterproofing\": \"Water barrier below slab per BES-21\",\n        \"wall_waterproofing\": \"Below grade foundation walls\",\n        \"air_water_barrier\": \"Fluid applied membrane per wall sections\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Waterproofing at slab on grade and below grade walls. Air/water barrier is part of building envelope. Below-grade waterproofing estimated based on typical foundation depths.\"\n    },\n    \"07-02_building_insulation\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"07-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Building Insulation (Thermal)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 1680,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Wall areas x insulation layers + roof insulation\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"type\": \"2\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5)\", \"sf\": 485, \"location\": \"Exterior walls per BES-05, BES-10, BES-11\"},\n          {\"type\": \"3.5\\\" batt insulation (R-13)\", \"sf\": 485, \"location\": \"Wall cavities per BES-05, BES-10\"},\n          {\"type\": \"R-15 polyiso at slab edge\", \"sf\": 195, \"location\": \"2'-0\\\" from edge of slab per BES-21\"},\n          {\"type\": \"R-7.5 polyiso at foundation\", \"sf\": 145, \"location\": \"At face of foundation wall per BES-21\"},\n          {\"type\": \"R-33 polyiso roof insulation\", \"sf\": 485, \"description\": \"5.5\\\" min thickness at roof/canopy per BES-20\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Flute fill batt insulation\", \"sf\": 85, \"description\": \"Pack flute voids at new exterior walls per A-301\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_insulation_sf\": 1680\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"wall_insulation\": \"2\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5) + 3.5\\\" batt (R-13)\",\n        \"slab_insulation\": \"R-15 polyiso 2'-0\\\" from edge, R-7.5 at foundation face\",\n        \"roof_insulation\": \"R-33 polyiso (5.5\\\" min) per BES-20\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple insulation types per wall and roof assemblies. R-values specified per BES wall types. Roof insulation R-33 for PMMA roofing system.\"\n    },\n    \"07-03_roofing\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"07-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Roofing (PMMA System)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 485,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Canopy roof area from dimensions\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"area\": \"Canopy roof area\", \"sf\": 485, \"dimensions\": \"Approximately 37' x 18' per grid spacing\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Roof Type 1 per BES-20\", \"description\": \"PMMA roofing, cover board, R-33 poly-iso insulation\"},\n          {\"slope\": \"1/4\\\" per foot cricket slope typical per A-501\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"roof_type\": \"BES-20: PMMA Roofing\",\n        \"components\": \"PMMA roofing, cover board, R-33 poly-iso insulation, existing SBS vapor barrier\",\n        \"slope\": \"1/4\\\" per ft slope to drains\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"New roofing at canopy area only. Connects to existing roof at building wall. Cricket slopes for drainage per A-501. PMMA (polymethyl methacrylate) liquid applied roofing.\"\n    },\n    \"07-04_firestopping\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"07-04\",\n      \"description\": \"Firestopping\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for firestopping system\",\n        \"locations\": [\n          {\"location\": \"Penetrations through rated walls\", \"description\": \"MEP penetrations through BES-05, BES-10 walls\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Penetrations through roof\", \"description\": \"Roof drains, vents, equipment\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Floor/slab penetrations\", \"description\": \"Conduit sleeves through grade beams and slab\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Curtain wall perimeter\", \"description\": \"Firestopping at slab edge and storefront\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"rating\": \"Per code and fire rated assemblies\",\n        \"materials\": \"Intumescent sealant, firestop pillows, mortar as required\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Firestopping required at all penetrations through rated assemblies. Hospital occupancy requires strict firestopping compliance.\"\n    },\n    \"07-05_joint_sealants\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"07-05\",\n      \"description\": \"Joint Sealants\",\n      \"unit\": \"LF\",\n      \"quantity\": 485,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Perimeter of building + control joints\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"type\": \"Sealant at storefront perimeters\", \"lf\": 165, \"description\": \"Interior and exterior storefront systems\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Sealant at door frames\", \"lf\": 95, \"description\": \"HM and aluminum door frames\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Control joints in slab\", \"lf\": 125, \"description\": \"Construction joints, isolation joints per FO-200\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Expansion joints at walls\", \"lf\": 65, \"description\": \"Wall to wall, wall to existing connections\"},\n          {\"type\": \"Roof expansion joints\", \"lf\": 35, \"description\": \"Canopy perimeters\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_lf\": 485\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"interior\": \"Sealant and backer rod, typ both sides per details\",\n        \"exterior\": \"Double layer (waterproofing + weathering) of sealant\",\n        \"elastomeric\": \"+/- 50% joint movement, color to match brick\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Extensive sealant requirements per A-301 details. Elastomeric sealant at masonry joints. Double layer sealant at exterior conditions.\"\n    },\n    \"31-01_site_excavation\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"31-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Excavation\",\n      \"unit\": \"CY\",\n      \"quantity\": 95,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Foundation footprint x depth + area excavation\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"area\": \"Foundation excavation for pile caps and grade beams\", \"sf\": 485, \"depth\": \"3'-0\\\"\", \"cy\": 54},\n          {\"area\": \"General site excavation for paving and utilities\", \"sf\": 820, \"depth\": \"1'-6\\\"\", \"cy\": 46}\n        ],\n        \"subtotal_cy\": 100,\n        \"shrinkage_factor\": 0.95,\n        \"adjusted_cy\": 95\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"dewatering\": \"Maintain groundwater 2 feet below excavation per FO-002\",\n        \"compaction\": \"95% standard proctor for backfill\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Limited civil drawings available. Excavation estimated from foundation plan FO-101 and typical site work. Verify quantities with civil drawings C-050 and C-101. Groundwater control required.\"\n    },\n    \"31-02_site_fill_grading\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"31-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Fill/Grading\",\n      \"unit\": \"CY\",\n      \"quantity\": 65,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Backfill around foundations + site grading fill\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"area\": \"Structural backfill around foundations\", \"sf\": 485, \"depth\": \"2'-6\\\"\", \"cy\": 45},\n          {\"area\": \"General site grading fill\", \"sf\": 520, \"depth\": \"1'-0\\\"\", \"cy\": 20}\n        ],\n        \"total_cy\": 65\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"compaction\": \"95% standard proctor per FO-002\",\n        \"material\": \"Select fill, free of organics and debris\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Backfill quantities estimated. Verify with civil drawings. Compaction to 95% required for structural fill.\"\n    },\n    \"32-01_asphalt_paving\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"32-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Asphalt Paving\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 1850,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"From A-101 proposed concrete & paving diagram and demo plan\",\n        \"areas\": [\n          {\"location\": \"Ambulance court resurfacing\", \"sf\": 1250, \"description\": \"Removal and replacement per C-050\"},\n          {\"location\": \"New ramp with asphalt\", \"sf\": 385, \"description\": \"Per A-102 equipment plan\"},\n          {\"location\": \"Access drive repairs\", \"sf\": 215, \"description\": \"Tie-ins and repairs\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 1850\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"thickness\": \"3\\\" binder + 2\\\" wearing surface typical\",\n        \"base\": \"Compacted aggregate base per civil specs\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Asphalt quantities estimated from demo plan notation 'Approximate scope of removal of asphalt, see civil dwgs'. Civil drawings not fully available for verification.\"\n    },\n    \"32-02_site_concrete\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"32-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Concrete (Curbs, Walks, Paving)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 650,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"New concrete areas from A-101 and estimated\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"item\": \"Concrete curbs (new)\", \"lf\": 145, \"width\": \"1'-0\\\"\", \"sf\": 145},\n          {\"item\": \"Concrete walks and paving\", \"sf\": 385, \"description\": \"New walks and paved areas\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Bollard foundations\", \"each\": 6, \"sf_each\": 4, \"sf\": 24},\n          {\"item\": \"Canopy foundations and piers\", \"sf\": 96, \"description\": \"Pile caps and grade beam extensions\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 650\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"concrete_strength\": \"4000 PSI\",\n        \"reinforcement\": \"#4 bars as required\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Site concrete includes curbs, walks, and paving not part of building. Civil drawings needed for accurate quantities.\"\n    },\n    \"32-03_site_utilities\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"32-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Utilities\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for site utility work\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"utility\": \"Storm water connections\", \"description\": \"Connect to existing system\"},\n          {\"utility\": \"Sanitary sewer connections\", \"description\": \"Cart wash and floor drain connections\"},\n          {\"utility\": \"Water service connections\", \"description\": \"Domestic water for cart wash, hose bibs\"},\n          {\"utility\": \"Gas service\", \"description\": \"If required for new equipment\"},\n          {\"utility\": \"Electrical site work\", \"description\": \"See Item 33-02\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Utility work scope unclear without civil drawings. Assumes connections only - new piping minimal for this addition. Verify scope with C-101 and MEP drawings.\"\n    },\n    \"32-04_erosion_control\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"32-04\",\n      \"description\": \"Erosion Control\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for erosion control measures\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"item\": \"Silt fence\", \"lf\": 185, \"description\": \"Perimeter protection\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Inlet protection\", \"each\": 4, \"description\": \"Storm drain protection\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Construction entrance\", \"each\": 1, \"description\": \"Stone stabilized entrance\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Dust control\", \"description\": \"Water truck, sweeping as needed\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"compliance\": \"NYC DEP and NYSDEC requirements\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Standard erosion control for urban hospital construction. Hospital setting requires strict sediment control.\"\n    },\n    \"33-01_storm_drainage\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"33-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Storm Drainage (Site)\",\n      \"unit\": \"LF\",\n      \"quantity\": 145,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Linear feet of drainage piping and structures\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\"item\": \"Roof drain leaders\", \"lf\": 65, \"size\": \"4\\\"-6\\\"\", \"description\": \"From canopy to grade\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Site storm piping\", \"lf\": 55, \"size\": \"6\\\"-8\\\"\", \"description\": \"Connections to existing\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Area drains and structures\", \"each\": 3, \"description\": \"Catch basins, drain boxes\"}\n        ],\n        \"total_lf\": 145\n      },\n      \"specs\": {\n        \"pipe_material\": \"PVC or ductile iron\",\n        \"connections\": \"Waterproof at building penetrations\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Storm drainage estimated from roof area and typical configurations. Canopy has roof drains per A-303. Verify with civil C-102.\"\n    },\n    \"33-02_site_electrical\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"33-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Electrical\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum for site electrical work\",\n        \"components\": [\n          {\"item\": \"Exterior lighting\", \"description\": \"Security lighting at canopy and entrance\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Power for equipment\", \"description\": \"Camera poles, security equipment\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Emergency lighting\", \"description\": \"Exit signs, egress lighting\"},\n          {\"item\": \"Conduit runs\", \"lf\": 125, \"description\": \"Underground conduit for power\"},\n          {\"item\": \"HandWave plates and pedestals\", \"each\": 4, \"description\": \"Per A-102 equipment plan\"}\n        ]\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Site electrical includes exterior lighting, security equipment power, and connections. Equipment locations per A-102.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_items\": 21,\n    \"high_confidence\": 2,\n    \"medium_confidence\": 12,\n    \"low_confidence\": 7\n  },\n  \"data_sources\": [\n    \"FO-101 Foundation Plan (page_114)\",\n    \"FO-200, FO-201, FO-300 Foundation Details (pages_115-117)\",\n    \"FO-002 Foundation General Notes (page_113)\",\n    \"S-101 Canopy Framing Plan (page_121)\",\n    \"A-101 Construction Plan (page_009)\",\n    \"A-200 Exterior Components (page_011)\",\n    \"A-221 Building Section (page_012)\",\n    \"A-223/A-224 Wall Sections (page_014)\",\n    \"A-301 Exterior Details (page_016)\",\n    \"A-303 Roof Details (page_018)\",\n    \"A-501 RCP and Roof Plan (page_021)\",\n    \"BES Wall Types from A-200\"\n  ],\n  \"key_assumptions\": [\n    \"Foundation volumes calculated from FO-101 plan and FO-300 sections\",\n    \"Structural steel quantities estimated from S-101 framing plan with standard steel weights\",\n    \"Canopy area approximately 37' x 18' = 485 SF based on grid spacing\",\n    \"Masonry quantities based on wall types BES-05, BES-10, BES-11"},"partialArgs":"{\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"project\\\": \\\"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\\\",\\n  \\\"project_number\\\": \\\"11202402\\\",\\n  \\\"takeoff_batch\\\": \\\"BATCH 2 - STRUCTURAL, CIVIL & SITE\\\",\\n  \\\"extraction_date\\\": \\\"2026-02-02\\\",\\n  \\\"prepared_by\\\": \\\"Clawdbot Quantity Surveyor\\\",\\n  \\\"items\\\": {\\n    \\\"03-01_concrete_foundations\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"03-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Concrete Foundations (Pile Caps, Grade Beams, Slab)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"CY\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 42.5,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Sum of concrete volumes from FO-101 Foundation Plan and FO-300 Sections\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"item\\\": \\\"Pile Cap PC-1\\\",\\n            \\\"quantity\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"Varies per plan\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": \\\"2'-0\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"volume_cy\\\": 12.0,\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"4 pile caps @ ~3 CY each per FO-300 Detail 4\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"item\\\": \\\"Grade Beam GB-1\\\",\\n            \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"linear_feet\\\": 49,\\n            \\\"width\\\": \\\"1'-0\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": \\\"1'-6\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"volume_cy\\\": 2.7,\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"49 LF x 1' x 1.5' = 73.5 CF / 27\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"item\\\": \\\"Grade Beam GB-2\\\",\\n            \\\"quantity\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"linear_feet\\\": 38,\\n            \\\"width\\\": \\\"1'-0\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": \\\"1'-6\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"volume_cy\\\": 4.2,\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"38 LF total x 1' x 1.5' = 57 CF / 27\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"item\\\": \\\"Slab on Grade (Foundation)\\\",\\n            \\\"area_sf\\\": 592,\\n            \\\"thickness\\\": \\\"12\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"volume_cy\\\": 21.9,\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"592 SF x 1' = 592 CF / 27 per FO-101 Note 1\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"item\\\": \\\"Footing DB-1 (Dowel Beam)\\\",\\n            \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"linear_feet\\\": 18,\\n            \\\"width\\\": \\\"1'-0\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"depth\\\": \\\"1'-0\\\"\\\",\\n            \\\"volume_cy\\\": 0.7,\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"18 LF x 1' x 1' = 18 CF / 27\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_concrete_cy\\\": 42.5\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"concrete_strength\\\": \\\"4000 PSI at 28 days\\\",\\n        \\\"reinforcement\\\": \\\"Grade 60, ASTM A615, #4 to #11 bars per schedule\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Foundation plan FO-101 shows pile caps, grade beams, and slab. Volume calculated from plan dimensions and FO-300 sections. Some grade beam lengths estimated from grid spacing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"03-02_concrete_slab_on_grade\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"03-02\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Concrete Slab on Grade (Interior)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 592,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Room areas from A-101 Construction Plan\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"room\\\": \\\"CART WASH\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"16'-9 1/4\\\\\\\" x 12'-8 1/4\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 212},\\n          {\\\"room\\\": \\\"SECURITY STATION\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"12'-8 1/4\\\\\\\" x 6'-6 1/4\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 82},\\n          {\\\"room\\\": \\\"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"6'-3 1/4\\\\\\\" x 7'-11 1/2\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 50},\\n          {\\\"room\\\": \\\"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"18'-9 1/4\\\\\\\" x 11'-0 1/2\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 207},\\n          {\\\"room\\\": \\\"CART ALCOVE\\\", \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"6'-6 1/4\\\\\\\" x 6'-3 1/4\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 41}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_sf\\\": 592\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"slab_thickness\\\": \\\"12\\\\\\\" per FO-101 Note 1 (foundation), 4-7\\\\\\\" typical elsewhere\\\",\\n        \\\"concrete_strength\\\": \\\"4000 PSI\\\",\\n        \\\"reinforcement\\\": \\\"#6@12\\\\\\\" OC continuous top and bottom mat per FO-101\\\",\\n        \\\"finish\\\": \\\"FF 25 / FL 25 per FO-002\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"HIGH\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Slab on grade Type 1 per BES-21 detail. 12\\\\\\\" thick with double mat reinforcing in foundation areas. Includes waterproofing membrane and R-15 polyiso insulation 2'-0\\\\\\\" from edge.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"03-03_concrete_paving\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"03-03\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Concrete Paving (Site/Ambulance Court)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 385,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Estimated from A-101 proposed concrete & paving diagram\\\",\\n        \\\"areas\\\": [\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"New curb and gutter at canopy perimeter\\\", \\\"estimated_sf\\\": 180},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Walkway and sidewalk improvements\\\", \\\"estimated_sf\\\": 145},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Miscellaneous site concrete\\\", \\\"estimated_sf\\\": 60}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_sf\\\": 385\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"Site concrete per civil drawings (not fully available)\\\",\\n        \\\"thickness\\\": \\\"6\\\\\\\" typical for sidewalks, 8\\\\\\\" for vehicular areas\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"LOW\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Civil drawings C-101, C-102 not fully available in the drawing set. Quantity estimated from A-101 concrete diagram and typical ambulance bay configurations. Verify with civil drawings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"04-01_unit_masonry\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"04-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Unit Masonry (Brick and CMU walls)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 485,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Wall area from wall sections and exterior elevations\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"wall_type\\\": \\\"BES-05: Brick on CFMF stud exterior wall\\\",\\n            \\\"area_sf\\\": 280,\\n            \\\"components\\\": \\\"Brick, 1\\\\\\\" air space, R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, exterior sheathing, 8\\\\\\\" CFMF stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"wall_type\\\": \\\"BES-10: Brick on CMU exterior wall\\\",\\n            \\\"area_sf\\\": 145,\\n            \\\"components\\\": \\\"Brick, 1\\\\\\\" air space, R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, 6\\\\\\\" CMU, 3-5/8\\\\\\\" metal stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"wall_type\\\": \\\"BES-11: Insulated existing exterior wall\\\",\\n            \\\"area_sf\\\": 60,\\n            \\\"components\\\": \\\"R-8.5 poly-iso, air/water membrane, 3-5/8\\\\\\\" metal stud with R-13 batt, GYP BD\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_sf\\\": 485\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"brick\\\": \\\"To match existing color/coursing\\\",\\n        \\\"cmu\\\": \\\"6\\\\\\\" CMU per BES-10\\\",\\n        \\\"insulation\\\": \\\"2\\\\\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5) + 3.5\\\\\\\" batt (R-13)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"New brick walls per A-221 building elevations to match existing. BES-05 and BES-10 wall types from A-200. Some existing walls receive insulation (BES-11).\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"05-01_structural_steel_framing\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"05-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Structural Steel Framing (Canopy and Supports)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LB\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 8750,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Steel takeoff from S-101 Canopy Framing Plan\\\",\\n        \\\"members\\\": [\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"W8X35\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 15, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 2100, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Primary canopy beams\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"W8X24\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 6, \\\"length_ft\\\": 12, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 1150, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Secondary beams\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"W8X10\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 8, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 320, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Light framing\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"HSS6X6X5/8\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 16, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 1280, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Main canopy posts (P1)\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"HSS6X4X3/8\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 2, \\\"length_ft\\\": 12, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 380, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Secondary posts\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"HSS4X4X3/8\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 10, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 480, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Minor posts\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"C8X13.75\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 8, \\\"length_ft\\\": 10, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 1100, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Canopy edge channels\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"C6X13\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 6, \\\"length_ft\\\": 8, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 625, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Secondary channels\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"L3X3X1/2\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 6, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 185, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Bracing angles\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"L2X2X3/16\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 5, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 52, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Light bracing\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"2L4X4X1/2X3/8\\\", \\\"quantity\\\": 4, \\\"length_ft\\\": 8, \\\"weight_lb\\\": 840, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Double angle connections\\\"},\\n          {\\\"member\\\": \\\"Misc connections and plates\\\", \\\"estimated_lb\\\": 738}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"subtotal_lb\\\": 9950,\\n        \\\"adjustment_factor\\\": 0.88,\\n        \\\"adjusted_total_lb\\\": 8750\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"steel_grade\\\": \\\"A992 or A572 Gr 50 for W-shapes, A500 for HSS\\\",\\n        \\\"connections\\\": \\\"Shear V=15 KIPS, Moment M=35 KIP-FT per S-101 notes\\\",\\n        \\\"top_of_steel_elevation\\\": \\\"27'-2\\\\\\\" TYP per S-101\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Steel quantities estimated from S-101 Canopy Framing Plan. Member counts and lengths approximate based on plan dimensions. Existing steel (E)W shapes are existing to remain. New steel is approximately 8,750 lbs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"05-02_metal_canopy\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"05-02\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Metal Canopy (Emergency Entrance)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LS\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Lump Sum for complete canopy system\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": [\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Structural steel frame (new)\\\", \\\"reference\\\": \\\"Item 05-01\\\", \\\"notes\\\": \\\"~8,750 lbs new steel\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Metal roof deck\\\", \\\"area_sf\\\": 485, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Over canopy framing\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Roofing system\\\", \\\"reference\\\": \\\"Item 07-03\\\", \\\"notes\\\": \\\"PMMA roofing, R-33 insulation\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Fascia and soffit\\\", \\\"linear_ft\\\": 78, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Metal panel ceiling at canopy underside\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Gutters and downspouts\\\", \\\"linear_ft\\\": 42, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Perimeter drainage\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Connections to existing\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Attachment to existing W27x84 and W27x146 beams\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"canopy_dimensions\\\": {\\n          \\\"approximate_width\\\": \\\"37'-0\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n          \\\"approximate_depth\\\": \\\"18'-0\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n          \\\"area_sf\\\": 485,\\n          \\\"top_of_steel\\\": \\\"27'-2\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n          \\\"top_of_slab\\\": \\\"28'-7 1/2\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Canopy spans from existing building to new steel posts per S-101. Area estimated from grid spacing (37' x 18' approximately). Includes structural frame, decking, roofing, and finishes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"05-03_miscellaneous_metal\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"05-03\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Miscellaneous Metal\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LS\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Lump Sum for miscellaneous metal items\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": [\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Shelf angles for brick support\\\", \\\"linear_ft\\\": 145, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Per wall sections A-223/A-224\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Lintel angles above openings\\\", \\\"each\\\": 6, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Over doors and storefront\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"HSS posts for storefront/doors\\\", \\\"each\\\": 4, \\\"size\\\": \\\"4.5\\\\\\\" x 4.5\\\\\\\" aluminum clad per A-223\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Steel tubes for wall framing\\\", \\\"linear_ft\\\": 85, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Various sizes per structure\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Bollards\\\", \\\"each\\\": 6, \\\"description\\\": \\\"New bollards per A-101\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Flood barrier system\\\", \\\"each\\\": 1, \\\"description\\\": \\\"High-performance flood barrier per A-101 Keynote A1\\\"}\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Miscellaneous metal includes structural support elements not in main frame, masonry supports, door hardware, and site elements.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"06-01_rough_carpentry\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"06-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Rough Carpentry (Wood blocking, framing)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LS\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Lump Sum for wood framing and blocking\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": [\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"FR wood blocking for storefront\\\", \\\"bf\\\": 85, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Fire-retardant blocking at door frames per A-301\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Wood blocking for equipment\\\", \\\"bf\\\": 45, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Security equipment, camera mounts\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Blocking for casework/millwork\\\", \\\"bf\\\": 30, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Security station counters\\\"},\\n          {\\\"component\\\": \\\"Furring and miscellaneous\\\", \\\"bf\\\": 40, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Various conditions\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_bf\\\": 200\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"material\\\": \\\"Fire-retardant treated lumber (FR)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"LOW\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Limited wood blocking per details. Most framing is CFMF studs. Fire-retardant treatment required per code for hospital occupancy.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"07-01_waterproofing\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"07-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Waterproofing (Below grade and roofing)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 925,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Slab area + wall below grade areas\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Slab on grade waterproofing membrane\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 592, \\\"description\\\": \\\"BES-21: Water barrier below slab\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Foundation wall waterproofing\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 285, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Exterior of foundation walls below grade, 2'-6\\\\\\\" avg height x 114 LF\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Air/Water barrier on walls\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Fluid applied air/water barrier per wall sections\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_sf\\\": 925\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"slab_waterproofing\\\": \\\"Water barrier below slab per BES-21\\\",\\n        \\\"wall_waterproofing\\\": \\\"Below grade foundation walls\\\",\\n        \\\"air_water_barrier\\\": \\\"Fluid applied membrane per wall sections\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Waterproofing at slab on grade and below grade walls. Air/water barrier is part of building envelope. Below-grade waterproofing estimated based on typical foundation depths.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"07-02_building_insulation\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"07-02\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Building Insulation (Thermal)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1680,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Wall areas x insulation layers + roof insulation\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"2\\\\\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5)\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"location\\\": \\\"Exterior walls per BES-05, BES-10, BES-11\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"3.5\\\\\\\" batt insulation (R-13)\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"location\\\": \\\"Wall cavities per BES-05, BES-10\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"R-15 polyiso at slab edge\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 195, \\\"location\\\": \\\"2'-0\\\\\\\" from edge of slab per BES-21\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"R-7.5 polyiso at foundation\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 145, \\\"location\\\": \\\"At face of foundation wall per BES-21\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"R-33 polyiso roof insulation\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"description\\\": \\\"5.5\\\\\\\" min thickness at roof/canopy per BES-20\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Flute fill batt insulation\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 85, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pack flute voids at new exterior walls per A-301\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_insulation_sf\\\": 1680\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"wall_insulation\\\": \\\"2\\\\\\\" continuous polyiso (R-8.5) + 3.5\\\\\\\" batt (R-13)\\\",\\n        \\\"slab_insulation\\\": \\\"R-15 polyiso 2'-0\\\\\\\" from edge, R-7.5 at foundation face\\\",\\n        \\\"roof_insulation\\\": \\\"R-33 polyiso (5.5\\\\\\\" min) per BES-20\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Multiple insulation types per wall and roof assemblies. R-values specified per BES wall types. Roof insulation R-33 for PMMA roofing system.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"07-03_roofing\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"07-03\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Roofing (PMMA System)\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 485,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Canopy roof area from dimensions\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": [\\n          {\\\"area\\\": \\\"Canopy roof area\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"dimensions\\\": \\\"Approximately 37' x 18' per grid spacing\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Roof Type 1 per BES-20\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"PMMA roofing, cover board, R-33 poly-iso insulation\\\"},\\n          {\\\"slope\\\": \\\"1/4\\\\\\\" per foot cricket slope typical per A-501\\\"}\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"roof_type\\\": \\\"BES-20: PMMA Roofing\\\",\\n        \\\"components\\\": \\\"PMMA roofing, cover board, R-33 poly-iso insulation, existing SBS vapor barrier\\\",\\n        \\\"slope\\\": \\\"1/4\\\\\\\" per ft slope to drains\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"New roofing at canopy area only. Connects to existing roof at building wall. Cricket slopes for drainage per A-501. PMMA (polymethyl methacrylate) liquid applied roofing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"07-04_firestopping\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"07-04\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Firestopping\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LS\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Lump Sum for firestopping system\\\",\\n        \\\"locations\\\": [\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Penetrations through rated walls\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"MEP penetrations through BES-05, BES-10 walls\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Penetrations through roof\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Roof drains, vents, equipment\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Floor/slab penetrations\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Conduit sleeves through grade beams and slab\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Curtain wall perimeter\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Firestopping at slab edge and storefront\\\"}\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"rating\\\": \\\"Per code and fire rated assemblies\\\",\\n        \\\"materials\\\": \\\"Intumescent sealant, firestop pillows, mortar as required\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Firestopping required at all penetrations through rated assemblies. Hospital occupancy requires strict firestopping compliance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"07-05_joint_sealants\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"07-05\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Joint Sealants\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"LF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 485,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Perimeter of building + control joints\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Sealant at storefront perimeters\\\", \\\"lf\\\": 165, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Interior and exterior storefront systems\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Sealant at door frames\\\", \\\"lf\\\": 95, \\\"description\\\": \\\"HM and aluminum door frames\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Control joints in slab\\\", \\\"lf\\\": 125, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Construction joints, isolation joints per FO-200\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Expansion joints at walls\\\", \\\"lf\\\": 65, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wall to wall, wall to existing connections\\\"},\\n          {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Roof expansion joints\\\", \\\"lf\\\": 35, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Canopy perimeters\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_lf\\\": 485\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"interior\\\": \\\"Sealant and backer rod, typ both sides per details\\\",\\n        \\\"exterior\\\": \\\"Double layer (waterproofing + weathering) of sealant\\\",\\n        \\\"elastomeric\\\": \\\"+/- 50% joint movement, color to match brick\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"MEDIUM\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Extensive sealant requirements per A-301 details. Elastomeric sealant at masonry joints. Double layer sealant at exterior conditions.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"31-01_site_excavation\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"31-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Site Excavation\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"CY\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 95,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Foundation footprint x depth + area excavation\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"area\\\": \\\"Foundation excavation for pile caps and grade beams\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"depth\\\": \\\"3'-0\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"cy\\\": 54},\\n          {\\\"area\\\": \\\"General site excavation for paving and utilities\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 820, \\\"depth\\\": \\\"1'-6\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"cy\\\": 46}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"subtotal_cy\\\": 100,\\n        \\\"shrinkage_factor\\\": 0.95,\\n        \\\"adjusted_cy\\\": 95\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"dewatering\\\": \\\"Maintain groundwater 2 feet below excavation per FO-002\\\",\\n        \\\"compaction\\\": \\\"95% standard proctor for backfill\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"LOW\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Limited civil drawings available. Excavation estimated from foundation plan FO-101 and typical site work. Verify quantities with civil drawings C-050 and C-101. Groundwater control required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"31-02_site_fill_grading\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"31-02\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Site Fill/Grading\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"CY\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 65,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"Backfill around foundations + site grading fill\\\",\\n        \\\"breakdown\\\": [\\n          {\\\"area\\\": \\\"Structural backfill around foundations\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 485, \\\"depth\\\": \\\"2'-6\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"cy\\\": 45},\\n          {\\\"area\\\": \\\"General site grading fill\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 520, \\\"depth\\\": \\\"1'-0\\\\\\\"\\\", \\\"cy\\\": 20}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"total_cy\\\": 65\\n      },\\n      \\\"specs\\\": {\\n        \\\"compaction\\\": \\\"95% standard proctor per FO-002\\\",\\n        \\\"material\\\": \\\"Select fill, free of organics and debris\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"LOW\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Backfill quantities estimated. Verify with civil drawings. Compaction to 95% required for structural fill.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"32-01_asphalt_paving\\\": {\\n      \\\"item_code\\\": \\\"32-01\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Asphalt Paving\\\",\\n      \\\"unit\\\": \\\"SF\\\",\\n      \\\"quantity\\\": 1850,\\n      \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n        \\\"method\\\": \\\"From A-101 proposed concrete & paving diagram and demo plan\\\",\\n        \\\"areas\\\": [\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Ambulance court resurfacing\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 1250, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Removal and replacement per C-050\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"New ramp with asphalt\\\", \\\"sf\\\": 385, \\\"description\\\": \\\"Per A-102 equipment plan\\\"},\\n          {\\\"location\\\": \\\"Access drive repairs\\\", \\\"sf\\\"